  "body": "The parent #4271 is merged (`ec314174e`); this PR now shows only its own commits.\n\n## What changed\n\nThis PR closes the three open items that #4271 listed for the tool library window (U7).\n\n1. **Built-in ER collets.** `component_library::builtins` now holds 89 metric ER collets (ER11 to ER40). The bores come from the ER table that the holder library already has (`holder_library::ER_SIZES`, ISO 15488 series, DIN 6499 collet ranges). There is one collet for each whole millimetre. Each collet is an adaptive item: machine side `ER<n>`, tool side `CYL <bore>`. The existing fit rule then gives the pairs, and no new rule is necessary:\n   - a built-in `BT40 ER32` chuck takes each ER32 collet and no other collet;\n   - the `ER32 collet 12 mm` takes each straight shank of 12 mm.\n\n   \"Show compatible parts\" on a built-in solid tool now lists its collets.\n2. **Stack values and swap.** The component stack group shows three read-only values from `tool_assembly::derive`: the gauge length, the cutting diameter and the corner radius. If the stack does not resolve, the group shows the refusal of the resolver. Each row has a \"Swap <part>…\" menu. The menu lists only the parts with which the whole stack still resolves. A pick lands the new stack as one `SetToolAssembly` (one undo step). The swap is available on the applied stack only. A new cache (`stack_view`) builds the offer, the values and the swap lists when the stack changes. A still frame builds nothing.\n3. **Test gap.** A test now clicks through the \"Add component\" combo box, then clicks \"Apply stack\".\n\nThe decisions are in `docs/decisions/3898-tool-library-components-2.md`.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n- `camcraft-app` `tool_library_holders`:\n  - `builtin_collets::each_er_series_has_a_collet_for_each_whole_millimetre`\n  - `builtin_collets::a_built_in_er_chuck_takes_its_collets_and_a_collet_takes_its_shank`\n  - `builtin_collets::a_built_in_chuck_collet_and_tool_resolve_to_the_tool_with_its_gauge`\n- `camcraft-ui` lib, `egui_app::tests::tool_library_stack`:\n  - `the_add_component_combo_box_builds_the_stack_and_apply_lands_it`\n  - `the_stack_shows_the_resolved_gauge_diameter_and_corner_or_the_refusal`\n  - `a_swap_offers_only_parts_that_resolve_and_is_one_undo_step`\n  - `a_still_frame_builds_no_stack_view`\n  - `show_compatible_parts_on_a_built_in_tool_lists_its_collets`\n\n## Gate results (head 5300e9187)\n\n- Quick gate, macOS, `cargo xtask gate quick --base 8edfca4bd46c3cfbc7a8bd42756721b800710d97`: 13 steps, 0 failed (app lib, app `tool_library_holders`, ui lib and 8 ui suites).\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- Light lane, macOS, `cargo xtask gate light`: 6 steps, 0 failed.\n- `camcraft-ui` lib tests on Windows (winbuild): 1726 passed, 0 failed, 8 ignored.\n- The example catalog suites are not necessary: no post and no toolpath changed.\n- The `#[test]` count of `crates/ui` goes up by 5. No snapshot PNG changed.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- A turning tool stack. It needs the lathe resolver caller of #3643.\n- Shanks that are not a whole millimetre (inch shanks, drill shanks) find no built-in collet. The fit rule compares exact bores. Follow-up: #4274 (a collet clamps a range).\n- MCP tools for the component commands stay on #3647. The swap uses the existing `SetToolAssembly` command, so it adds no new command.\n\nChangelog: The tool library has built-in ER collets (ER11 to ER40), so a built-in ER chuck, a collet and a built-in solid tool make a tool stack. The component stack shows the gauge length, the cutting diameter and the corner radius of the stack, and \"Swap\" puts a part that fits in the place of one part, in one undo step.\n\nEffort: high\n\nRefs #3898\nRefs #3648\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n\n\n## Screenshots\n\nThe images come from the headless test renderer. Before is the head of #4271 (`d354110da`). After is head `cfc5d2c0f`.\n\n**Component stack group**\n\nBefore: the group shows the stack rows only.\n\n![before: stack group](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qsmits/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/4280/4-before-stack-group.png)\n\nAfter: the group shows Gauge length, Cutting diameter and Corner radius, and a \"Swap <part>...\" button on each row.\n\n![after: stack group with resolved values](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qsmits/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/4280/4-after-stack-values.png)\n\nAfter: the menu \"Swap fly-25...\" offers only the part with which the stack still resolves.\n\n![after: swap menu open](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qsmits/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/4280/4-after-swap-menu.png)\n\nAn unapplied stack edit: the group shows the note \"(from the stack edits; not applied)\". The swap buttons are disabled. The tooltip says \"apply or undo the stack edits first\".\n\n![draft stack: unapplied note and disabled swap buttons](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qsmits/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/4280/6-draft-stack-unapplied.png)\n\n**Show compatible parts on a built-in tool**\n\nBefore: the tool EM-1200-2FL gives an empty result.\n\n![before: no component matches](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qsmits/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/4280/5-before-compatible-empty.png)\n\nAfter: the result lists the ER collets of its shank.\n\n![after: ER collets listed](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qsmits/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/4280/5-after-compatible-collets.png)\n\n\n",
